# The organisation's repositories (github.com/veranda-x16; DECISIONS V139,
# docs/PUBLISHING.md), read by tools/publish.sh and the CI templates.
#
# One line a repository, fields separated by " | ":
#   repo      the repository's name in the organisation
#   tree      its source here: "." (this tree) or a folder under
#             $VERANDA_PROJECTS (default ~/Projects)
#   key       its name in a release tag's BUILT FROM (tools/mkdist.sh's
#             refs.txt: the tree's folder name)
#   refs      the refs tools/mkdist.sh builds (the first that exists), for
#             a test publish; a release uses the commit its BUILT FROM names
#   mode      export: git archive of that commit, minus tools/publish.private,
#             one commit a publish ("Veranda <version>"); history: the
#             branch pushed with its history (upstream authors' commits kept);
#             own: kept by its own maintainers in the organisation (changes
#             go to them as patches; their own CI workflow): tools/publish.sh
#             never pushes it (publish.py repos leaves it out), but the
#             release builds it as a sibling at the release's tag
#             (.github/workflows/release.yml, test.yml; DECISIONS V203)
#   branch    the organisation's branch it goes to
#   licence   what its LICENSE / COPYING says (read: docs/PUBLISHING.md)
#   build     its CI build against Veranda's SDK ($SDK), from its top
#   output    the build's output (the CI checks it is there)
#
# NEVER here: geoWrite (veranda-geowrite) and TopDesk (veranda-topdesk),
# Berkeley Softworks' and GEOS-USER-CLUB's programs, ported for personal
# use; CommanderSID (SID Player is its own port, veranda-sidplay).
# tools/publish.sh refuses them by name even if a line names them.
#
# repo             | tree              | key               | refs           | mode    | branch  | licence                         | build                                      | output
veranda            | .                 | Veranda           | main           | export  | main    | MIT                             | -                                          | -
veranda-write      | commander-write   | commander-write   | main           | export  | main    | MIT                             | make veranda SDK=$SDK                      | build/veranda/Veranda Write.cvt
commander-calc     | commander-calc    | commander-calc    | layout veranda | export  | main    | MIT                             | make veranda SDK=$SDK                      | build/veranda/Veranda Calc.cvt
lighthouse-pinball | veranda-pinball   | veranda-pinball   | master         | export  | main    | MIT                             | make -C veranda SDK=$SDK                   | build/veranda/Lighthouse Pinball.cvt
harbour-walls      | harbour-walls     | harbour-walls     | master         | export  | main    | MIT                             | make SDK=$SDK                              | build/app/Harbour Walls.cvt
veranda-sidplay    | veranda-sidplay   | veranda-sidplay   | main           | export  | main    | GPL-3.0-or-later                | make build/app/app.cvt VSDK=$SDK           | build/app/app.cvt
veranda-solitaire  | veranda-solitaire | veranda-solitaire | main           | export  | main    | GPL-3.0-or-later                | make -C veranda SDK=$SDK                   | build/veranda/Veranda Solitaire.cvt
mod-player         | x16-mod           | x16-mod           | layout veranda | export  | main    | MIT; vendor/micromod-c BSD-3    | make veranda VSDK=$SDK                     | build/veranda/MOD Player.cvt
geochess           | veranda-geochess  | veranda-geochess  | veranda        | history | veranda | Scott Hutter's permission       | make -C veranda SDK=$SDK                   | build/veranda/geoChess.cvt
x16-emulator       | x16-emulator-modem | x16-emulator-modem | modem         | history | modem   | BSD-2-Clause (x16emu's)         | -                                          | -
veranda-prog8      | veranda-prog8     | veranda-prog8     | main           | own     | main    | MIT (Anthony W. Henry; Veranda's parts Marcin Spoczynski) | make VSDK=$SDK PROG8C="$PROG8C"           | template/app.cvt
vidkit-player      | vidkit-player     | vidkit-player     | main           | own     | main    | MIT (Anthony W. Henry; VIDKIT inside, his, MIT) | make P8KIT=$P8KIT VSDK=$SDK PROG8C="$PROG8C" | build/VIDKIT Player.cvt
